sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-09, containers reach models with only the placeholder key and no real key on their Node (ADR 0252).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · `ai-router:model-forwarder NODE` on the Gateway, once per agent Node, and with `--remove` to withdraw it
  %% kind: ai_router.model_forwarder
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane R icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant R as Router Node<br/>services, over ssh
  participant N as Agent Node<br/>beast, over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the forwarder<br/>the agent Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - renders the guard as `ai-router:task-guard` does, with the Node's WireGuard address added to its sources, or removed
  %%> - renders the forwarder's Caddyfile: the bridge address at port 8319, proxied unchanged to the guard origin; it holds no key
  %%> - pushes vault copies of the task key and the anchor key for the guard; the intent holds neither, and the forwarder gets neither
  %%> - takes the lock `ai_router_guard:<router Node>`, which guard runs share
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the ai-router extension is set up on its Node
  %%> - the guard is in place for an applying run: a forwarder run never brings back a removed guard
  %%> - the Node is active Linux with a WireGuard address, and is not the router's Node, the swamp Node or the vpn hub
  %%> - `--bridge` and `--address` name the container bridge and its IPv4 address; a removal reuses those of the last run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>ai_router.model_forwarder
  SW->>N: Install the forwarder<br/>Ansible
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - before the guard admits the Node, so a run that fails later leaves no Node admitted without its table; a removal installs nothing here
  %%> - checks that the address belongs to the bridge
  %%> - makes the forwarder's system user and loads its nftables table from a oneshot unit that starts early at boot, before WireGuard, Docker and Incus: forwarded packets to the guard are dropped ahead of Docker and UFW, and only the forwarder's user may connect to the guard from the Node
  %%> - runs its own Caddy, `orbit-ai-router-forwarder.service`, on the bridge address at port 8319, only while the table's unit is up: its own user, no admin endpoint, no saved config, no key
  %%> - waits for a listening socket on the bridge address at port 8319 without connecting from the Node, whose traffic enters over lo and is rejected
  %%> - allows port 8319 in on the bridge only
  SW->>R: Apply the guard<br/>Ansible
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the guard phase of `ai-router:task-guard`: keys, Caddyfile, unit, and the UFW allow of each forwarder Node above the deny; the allow of a Node the rules do not name goes
  %%> - its end checks: from the router Node and from the swamp Node, a source outside the admitted sources is refused
  %%> - a removal while the guard is off skips this phase and leaves the guard off
  SW->>N: Prove the path<br/>from the bridge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - from a namespace whose veth is a port of the bridge, as a container: a POST through the forwarder with no key gets the guard's 401, which it gives only to a source it admits
  %%> - from that namespace, a request straight to the guard fails and the forward drop counter rises
  %%> - from the Node as root, a request to the guard fails and the output reset counter rises
  %%> - `--remove`: takes the forwarder, its table, both units, its folder, its state, its UFW rule and its user off the Node, then checks that the router Node answers SSH and the guard port does not answer the Node
  alt the checks pass
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    Note over GW: Record the forwarder<br/>http://10.251.33.1:8319
    %%> Result:
    %%> - containers on the Node call this origin with the one task key; only the `agent` uid reaches it, by the container's own nftables rule
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
  end
